    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "description": "Jolie is the filtered showerhead people buy because it looks like a good showerhead first and a filter second. Retail listings describe a high-impact ABS head with a 1.8 gpm flow rating for California and New York compliance, a filter cartridge that sits in the neck, and a media mix of KDF-55 and calcium sulfite, two materials commonly used because they work in hot water. Jolie says its filter removes over 84% of chlorine through the life of the cartridge and describes that as exceeding the NSF-177 benchmark, but we did not find a certification listing, so treat it as a brand claim. Replacement cartridges are listed at about $33 to $38 and Jolie says to swap them every 90 days, which makes it one of the more expensive filters to run.",
    "pros": [
      "KDF-55 and calcium sulfite media suited to hot water",
      "1.8 gpm head meets California and New York limits",
