  },
  {
    "id": "canopy-filtered-showerhead",
    "name": "Canopy Filtered Showerhead",
    "badge": "Best for Chloramine Areas",
    "category": "Filtered Showerhead, Carbon, KDF and Calcium Sulfite",
    "amazonUrl": "#",
    "description": "Canopy is the pick if your utility uses chloramine instead of chlorine, because its media includes calcium sulfite, which Canopy says helps reduce both. Canopy lists three media types, granular activated carbon, copper-zinc (KDF) and calcium sulfite, and says the filter is tested to NSF-177 for chlorine reduction. Its site lists chloramine among the contaminants its ingredients have been shown to help reduce, with an asterisk noting the filter is not independently tested for every contaminant on that list, which is an honest disclosure most brands skip. Canopy says to replace the cartridge every 90 days, and ships a 1.8 gpm low-flow head with a high-flow restrictor depending on your state.",
