    "description": "The Culligan WSH-C125 is the inexpensive filter with a real certification behind it. Retailers describe it as certified by NSF International to NSF/ANSI 177 for reduction of free available chlorine, and Culligan's manual says to replace the WHR-140 cartridge about every six months or 10,000 gallons, whichever comes first. Culligan's data sheet lists a 2.5 gpm rated flow, though some listings say 2.0 gpm. It is not a beauty product: a review notes it does not remove lead or bacteria, and its bacteriostatic media limits growth on the media rather than treating the water. One retailer lists the showerhead as discontinued while still selling the cartridge, so check availability and confirm you can buy WHR-140 replacements before committing.",
