---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Home Improvement",
    tags: [
      "best shower head filter",
      "shower filter",
      "filtered shower head",
      "shower filter for hard water",
      "shower filter for chlorine"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best Shower Head <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Filters</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          Six filtered showerheads and inline shower filters, chosen on the certifications and media each maker lists, with a straight answer on the one thing most of them cannot do: soften hard water.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#aquasana-aq-4100"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            See the Picks
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Alex Rivers</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Home Improvement Editor</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="7.1k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#how-we-chose" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. How We Chose</a>
          <a href="#what-it-does" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. What a Shower Filter Can Do</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Our 6 Picks</a>
          <a href="#nsf-177" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. NSF/ANSI 177 Explained</a>
          <a href="#media" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. KDF, Sulfite and Vitamin C</a>
          <a href="#hard-water" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Hard Water</a>
          <a href="#fit" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Fit and Flow</a>
          <a href="#cartridge-cost" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Cartridge Life and Cost</a>
          <a href="#living-with-one" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Installing and Living With One</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">11. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          A shower filter does one job well: it reduces chlorine in hot, fast-moving water. That can make a real difference to how your skin, hair and bathroom smell after a shower on city water. What it does not do, despite what a lot of packaging implies, is soften hard water, and choosing a filter starts with being clear about that.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="how-we-chose" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. How We Chose
          </h2>

          <p>
            We did not lab-test these filters. We chose them by reading what each brand claims, which standard it cites, which media it uses and how long its cartridge lasts, then checking those claims against retailer listings and manuals. Shower filters are a category full of vague promises about skin and hair, so we gave the most weight to the claims that can actually be checked.
          </p>

          <p>
            The most important of those is NSF/ANSI 177, the standard written specifically for shower filtration systems. It covers reduction of free available chlorine. A filter certified to NSF/ANSI 177 has been verified by an accredited body; a filter tested to it has had testing done, usually commissioned by the brand. Both are better than nothing, and we say which applies to each pick.
          </p>

          <p>
            Next we looked at the media. Activated carbon, which does most of the work in a drinking-water filter, is commonly described as much less effective in hot, fast-moving shower water. The media you want in a shower are those used precisely because they work in hot water: KDF copper-zinc, calcium sulfite and vitamin C. Every pick here uses at least one of them.
          </p>

          <p>
            Finally we compared cartridge life and running cost, because a filter you stop replacing is just a plastic fitting. A cartridge that lasts a year at a reasonable price is worth more than a cheaper one you forget to change after three months.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="what-it-does" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What a Shower Filter Can and Cannot Do
          </h2>

          <p>
            A shower filter's real job is reducing chlorine, the disinfectant most US utilities add to tap water. Chlorine is what gives a hot shower a pool-like smell, and many people find it dries their skin and hair. A good shower filter can reduce it noticeably, and if chlorine bothers you, that is a worthwhile improvement.
          </p>

          <p>
            Many utilities use chloramine instead of chlorine, because it lasts longer in the pipes. Chloramine is harder to remove. KDF and ordinary carbon are commonly described as weak against it, while calcium sulfite and vitamin C are the media brands use when they claim chloramine reduction. If your utility's annual water report says chloramine, pick a filter built for it, like the Canopy, and expect a shorter cartridge life.
          </p>

          <p>
            What a shower filter cannot do is soften hard water. Hardness is dissolved calcium and magnesium, and removing it takes ion exchange in a water softener or reverse osmosis, neither of which fits in a showerhead. Some filters claim to reduce scale or improve hard water, but the physics does not allow a cartridge that size to remove meaningful hardness from gallons of water per minute.
          </p>

          <p>
            Shower filters are also not a fix for a rotten-egg smell, iron staining or sediment across the whole house. Those problems come from the water supply or the water heater and need treatment at the source; our guide to <a href="/why-does-my-water-smell-like-rotten-eggs/">why water smells like rotten eggs</a> explains how to tell which. And none of these filters makes shower water safe to drink if it is not already.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. Our 6 Picks
          </h2>

          <p>
            We researched these six from manufacturer specifications, published certifications and retailer listings, not from our own testing. A shower filter's performance depends heavily on your water's chlorine or chloramine level and temperature, so every capacity and chlorine claim below is attributed to the brand or retailer that makes it. Where a brand says its filter was tested to NSF/ANSI 177 rather than certified, we say so.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                    <span class="bg-[#FF4500] text-white w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-black">
                      {index + 1}
                    </span>
                    {productImages[product.id] && (
                      <img
                        src={productImages[product.id]}
                        alt={product.name}
                        loading="lazy"
                        width="40"
                        height="40"
                        class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-white object-contain p-1 shrink-0"
                      />
                    )}
                    <div>
                      <h3 class="text-white font-black text-lg leading-snug m-0"><span class="block text-[#38BDF8] text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 sm:hidden">{product.badge}</span>{product.name}</h3>
                      <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs">{product.category}</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                  <span class="bg-[#38BDF8]/20 text-[#38BDF8] px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold hidden sm:block">
                    {product.badge}
                  </span>
                </div>
                <div class="p-6">
                  {product.rating && product.reviewCount && (
                  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
                    <div class="flex text-yellow-400">
                      {[...Array(5)].map((_, i) => (
                        <svg
                          class={`w-4 h-4 ${i < Math.floor(product.rating) ? "fill-current" : "text-gray-200"}`}
                          xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                          viewBox="0 0 20 20"
